+// Stage 5, HDR scene only. Additive flames were authored for an 8-bit display:
+// their encoded colours add up and each channel clips at white, so a dense core
+// turns orange, yellow, then white (red clips first with the default 0x903020).
+// In the linear scene each particle adds its decoded colour without that clip,
+// so the sum keeps the red of one particle at any density. Here the flames alone
+// are summed encoded (the 8-bit sum, unclipped in FP16), then composed once:
+// the colour of the clipped sum, decoded (the SDR picture of the flame), times
+// max(sum, 1)^hdrflammepente. Below white this is exactly the SDR picture; above,
+// the core keeps the SDR hue and gains HDR luminance with its density.
+extern bool hdrout_flamefix_wanted();
